        "pageid": 27718524,
        "ns": 0,
        "title": "Michael Jackson: The Experience",
        "extract": "Michael Jackson: The Experience is a music video game based on Michael Jackson's songs. It was developed and published by Ubisoft, and was released for the Nintendo DS, PlayStation Portable, and Wii in November 2010, for the PlayStation 3's PlayStation Move and the Xbox 360's Kinect in April 2011, for the Nintendo 3DS in November 2011, for iOS devices exclusively in North America on 7 December 2011, and for PlayStation Vita in February 2012. The Japanese release on 8 December 2011 only revised the PlayStation 3, Xbox 360, and Wii consoles. \nThe game features many of Jackson's hits, such as \"Bad\", \"Thriller\", \"Beat It\", \"Billie Jean\", \"Smooth Criminal\", \"Black or White\", \"The Way You Make Me Feel\", etc. However, some songs like \"Man in the Mirror\" and \"P.Y.T. (Pretty Young Thing)\" are excluded, and there are no songs from the Motown era. Initial launches of the game included a limited edition replica of Jackson's sequined glove.\nThe Wii version sold 2 million copies in two months, not including Japanese sales, making it one of the best-selling Wii title games.",
